OL,3,GNEWSAJoanna Lumley joins vigil for
OL,4,ANepal flood victims
OL,5,
OL,6,FDame Joanna Lumley has shared her
OL,7,Fbelief that the "heartbreaking" flash
OL,8,Fflood in Nepal was caused by human
OL,9,Fbehaviour and climate change, as she
OL,10,Fjoined a vigil in south-east London to
OL,11,Fremember the victims.
OL,13,FAbout 50 people gathered at Panas
OL,14,FGurkha Restaurant in Blackheath on
OL,15,FThursday to observe a minute's silence,
OL,16,Flight candles and hold prayers.
OL,18,FThe actress, who has frequently visited
OL,19,FNepal and has strong ties with the
OL,20,FGurkha community, said the flood in the
OL,21,Fnorth of the country on 26 August could
OL,22,Fhave been predicted.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,324,320,200,140,0,100
